   "text": "Yes, you can change the bulb yourself. For your Neff B1ACE4HN0B, you need a standard 25W or 40W heat-resistant oven bulb with an SES (small Edison screw) cap, rated for at least 300°C. To replace it, ensure the oven is switched off and cool, then unscrew the old bulb from inside the cavity and screw in the new one. If the light still doesn't work after changing the bulb, there may be a fault with the lamp holder or wiring, which would require an engineer."
